// GradDraw — displace each vertex along the gradient of a scalar field,
// computed by forward-mode autodiff. Demonstrates the `grad(expr, var)`
// builtin (Wave 6): expr is any scalar expression of the float3 var, and
// grad returns float3 = (∂expr/∂var.x, ∂expr/∂var.y, ∂expr/∂var.z). Each
// emitter rewrites the expression into dual-number form inline, so all
// backends produce the same gradient. Here the field is a concentric
// ripple in object space; pushing along its gradient ridges the surface.

// Not in the SculptBrushes enum (compiler-only demo), so its `accumulable` bit is
// never dispatched. If promoted, exclude it from non-accumulate mode: grad() over
// v.co is incompatible with the base-read proxy (plans/nonAccumMode.md).
@brush("graddraw")
brush GradDraw {
  ctx float3 surfaceNo;

  vertex void apply(inout Vertex v) {
    float s = strength(v.co) * (1.0 - v.mask);
    if (s == 0.0) {
      continue;
    }
    float3 g = grad(sin(length(v.co) * 40.0), v.co);
    v.co += normalize(g) * s;
  }
}
